  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd the catalog case `turning/groove-part-off`.\nThe case contains an original mesh generator, a build script, an embedded project, an NC program, and a README.\nIt shows Groove Rough, Groove Finish, and Parting with the GT-0300 blade on the built-in Lathe.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had no focused example for groove roughing, groove finishing, and part-off.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `groove_part_off_case_posts_rough_finish_and_axis_release` failed before the case existed and passes with the case.\n- The pin checks operation order, the groove window, rough diameter 22.5, finish diameter 22, and part-off at X0 Z13.5.\n- The pin also opens the project outside the case directory and checks the embedded mesh.\n- Four mutations failed: missing NC, wrong rough diameter, wrong finish diameter, and an incomplete part-off endpoint.\n- Each restored fixture passed. This change adds no production guard.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all three steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check` reproduced all six cases.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog` passed all five tests.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nAdd one golden: `examples/catalog/turning/groove-part-off/groove-part-off.nc`.\nIts 110 lines contain lathe setup, rough and finish plunges at Z35 and Z38, and part-off pecks to X0 at Z13.5.\nThe rough plunges reach X22.5. The finish plunges reach X22.\nThe parting blade center is Z15. Orientation 2 posts its low edge at Z13.5.\nNo existing NC or CL golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machining or GUI session was run.\nThe catalog tool has no modeled holder body. The README states this limit.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. PR #2913 changes `example_catalog.rs`; this PR uses a separate test file.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: Add a reproducible turning example for groove roughing, groove finishing, and part-off.\n\nFixes #2864\n",
